+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use LRU (Least Recently Used) cache eviction with a 300-second time-to-live (TTL), which superseded the earlier LFU (Least Frequently Used) policy; this combines recency-based eviction with automatic expiration so that entries are evicted when least-recently accessed and never persist longer than 300 seconds.
